Trust the system CA store (/etc/ssl/certs, from ca-certificates) INSTEAD of the
roots compiled into bun, so a CA removed from ca-certificates (CVE-2026-111943,
eMudhra) stops being trusted without a bun rebuild. gominimal/pkgmgr-rs#1026.

At bun-v1.3.14 there is no upstream switch that does this:
  - us_get_default_ca_store() (packages/bun-usockets/src/crypto/root_certs.cpp)
    ALWAYS adds the compiled-in roots. --use-system-ca / NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA=1
    only add the system roots to them (a union), so a distrust never applies.
  - --use-openssl-ca is parsed (src/cli/Arguments.zig sets Bun__Node__CAStore)
    and then ignored: nothing outside Arguments.zig reads Bun__Node__CAStore.
  - Upstream fixed --use-openssl-ca in oven-sh/bun#46542 (b70684d7, merged
    2026-10-23) on the 1.4 line only, after the Rust rewrite; it does not apply
    here and series_pins holds bun on 1.3.

This patch:
  - Arguments.zig: Bun__Node__CAStore defaults to .system instead of .bundled,
    so it reads .bundled only after an explicit --use-bundled-ca. The CLI block
    that sets it runs only for run/test/auto commands; every other command (and
    a `bun build --compile` executable) keeps the default.
  - root_certs.cpp: the default store gets the system roots and OpenSSL's
    default paths, and the compiled-in roots only when (a) --use-bundled-ca, or
    (b) NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA is 0/false/no/off (the opt-out), or (c) the system
    store is empty (no ca-certificates), so bun keeps working rather than trust
    nothing. (a) and (b) are upstream's store exactly, where
    NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA=1 still adds the system roots. --use-openssl-ca leaves
    the compiled-in roots and the system loader out, as #46542 does.

Not changed: tls.rootCertificates and tls.getCACertificates('bundled') still
list the compiled-in roots; tls.getCACertificates('default') (src/js/node/tls.ts)
is computed in JS and still lists them too. Connections use the native store.
NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS is still added. NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA=0 wins over
--use-system-ca. Drop this patch once bun's own default replaces the bundled
store, or move to --use-openssl-ca on a release that carries #46542.

--- a/packages/bun-usockets/src/crypto/root_certs.cpp
+++ b/packages/bun-usockets/src/crypto/root_certs.cpp
@@ -2,7 +2,9 @@
 #include "./root_certs_header.h"
 #include "./internal/internal.h"
 #include <mutex>
+#include <stdint.h>
 #include <string.h>
+#include <strings.h>
 #include "./default_ciphers.h"
 
 // System-specific includes for certificate loading
@@ -23,18 +25,34 @@
 // Forward declarations for platform-specific functions
 // (Actual implementations are in platform-specific files)
 
-// External variable from Zig CLI arguments
-extern "C" bool Bun__Node__UseSystemCA;
+// minimal: the system CA store replaces the compiled-in roots by default.
+// Bun__Node__CAStore is Arguments.zig's BunCAStore, enum(u8) { bundled,
+// openssl, system }. This patch changes its default from .bundled to .system,
+// so it reads .bundled only after an explicit --use-bundled-ca.
+extern "C" uint8_t Bun__Node__CAStore;
+enum { MINIMAL_CA_BUNDLED = 0, MINIMAL_CA_OPENSSL = 1, MINIMAL_CA_SYSTEM = 2 };
 
+// minimal: NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA=0 (or false/no/off, which Bun's own env parser
+// also reads as false) opts out of the system-store default.
+static bool minimal_system_ca_opted_out() {
+  const char *v = getenv("NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA");
+  return v && (strcmp(v, "0") == 0 || strcasecmp(v, "false") == 0 ||
+               strcasecmp(v, "no") == 0 || strcasecmp(v, "off") == 0);
+}
+
+// minimal: upstream's store (compiled-in roots plus OpenSSL's default paths),
+// asked for with --use-bundled-ca or the NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA opt-out.
+static bool minimal_upstream_ca_store() {
+  return Bun__Node__CAStore == MINIMAL_CA_BUNDLED || minimal_system_ca_opted_out();
+}
+
 // Helper function to check if system CA should be used
-// Checks both CLI flag (--use-system-ca) and environment variable (NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA=1)
 static bool us_should_use_system_ca() {
-  // Check CLI flag first
-  if (Bun__Node__UseSystemCA) {
-    return true;
+  // minimal: on by default; --use-openssl-ca leaves it out.
+  if (!minimal_upstream_ca_store()) {
+    return Bun__Node__CAStore == MINIMAL_CA_SYSTEM;
   }
-  
-  // Check environment variable
+  // Upstream's store: NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA=1 still adds the system roots to it.
   const char *use_system_ca = getenv("NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA");
   return use_system_ca && strcmp(use_system_ca, "1") == 0;
 }
@@ -222,8 +240,18 @@
